{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use imported C-defined macros as constants."}],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Language Interoperability with C and C++","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Language-Interoperability-with-C-and-C++"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Using Imported C Macros in Swift","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift automatically imports simple, constant-like macros, declared with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#define"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directive, as global constants. Macros are imported when they use literals for string,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floating-point, or integer values, or use operators like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":">"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between literals or previously defined macros. This example defines some simple macros"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in a C header:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"occ","code":["#define FADE_ANIMATION_DURATION 0.35","#define VERSION_STRING \"2.2.10.0a\"","#define MAX_RESOLUTION 1268","","#define HALF_RESOLUTION (MAX_RESOLUTION \/ 2)","#define IS_HIGH_RES (MAX_RESOLUTION > 1024)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When imported into Swift, the macros in the above example are equivalent to these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant declarations:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let FADE_ANIMATION_DURATION = 0.35","let VERSION_STRING = \"2.2.10.0a\"","let MAX_RESOLUTION = 1268","","let HALF_RESOLUTION = 634","let IS_HIGH_RES = true"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Use-Functions-and-Generics-Instead-of-Complex-Macros","text":"Use Functions and Generics Instead of Complex Macros"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"C macros that are more complex than simple constant definitions have no counterpart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Swift. You use complex macros in C and Objective-C to avoid type-checking constraints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or to avoid retyping large amounts of boilerplate code. However, macros can make"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"debugging and refactoring difficult. In Swift, you can use functions and generics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to achieve the same results without any compromises."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift":{"title":"Customizing Your C Code for Swift","abstract":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" macro to group functions that have related behavior."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift":{"title":"Using Imported C Structs and Unions in Swift","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how Swift represents imported C structures and unions, including types with"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"bitfields and unnamed fields."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"title":"Swift","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swift"}}}